{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1164981-the-list-of-ephemera","id":1164981,"title":"The List of Ephemera","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-04T00:10:47-08:00","id":1164981,"title":"The List of Ephemera","content":"So i want to assemble a list of all the Ephemeral beings in Chronicles of Darkness, so we can have a sensible list to reference.<br /> <br /> So we have at least<br /> <br /> Angels: Living God Machine Equations that serve as it's primary enforcers in the world and they are tied to Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> Spirits: Beings of the Shadow which are the spiritual representations of concepts, lifeforms or material objects((i count rocks and mountains in this category))<br /> <br /> Ghosts: Imprints of those who have died which are tied to the underworld.<br /> <br /> I know for a fact that there are more than these three, so if we can gather and define them here that would be great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T00:50:26-08:00","id":1164984,"title":"","content":"Goetia: Living images, icons, and ideas dreamt from minds, natives of the Astral Realms. <br /> <br /> Diaboli: Ephemeral entities corrupted by the Inferno. Immundi are Infernal spirits, Larvals are Infernal ghosts, and Deceptors are Infernal Goetia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T01:33:46-08:00","id":1164986,"title":"","content":"Most likely hedge ghosts from CtL 2e. I don't remember if they're explicitly ephemeral from the preview (using phone right now) but they're using ephemeral rules.<br /> <br /> Quashmallim from PtC and Supernal entities from MtA also use ephemeral rules, but are explicitly not ephemeral. Just thought it bears mentioning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T05:15:23-08:00","id":1165014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1164981-the-list-of-ephemera?p=1164986#post1164986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Quashmallim from PtC and Supernal entities from MtA also use ephemeral rules, but are explicitly not ephemeral. Just thought it bears mentioning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you could include Acamoth and Gulmoth (Astral and Spiritual Abyssal entities) in that category too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T10:28:51-08:00","id":1165091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1164981-the-list-of-ephemera?p=1164986#post1164986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most likely hedge ghosts from CtL 2e. I don't remember if they're explicitly ephemeral from the preview (using phone right now) but they're using ephemeral rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, they have PFR Traits and Influences, treat their Wyrd like a Rank stat for the purpose of resisting binding, and have common powers that roughly translate to specific Manifestation effects.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, they don't actually have Manifestations or a scaling capacity for manifestation, they weaken more drastically on Earth and suffer less direct pressure to leave it, and they specifically don't inhabit Twilight in their incorporeal state.<br /> <br /> They're Hedge-analogs for any given type of ephemeral being, but they only partially interact with the things that define a being as ephemeral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T16:27:23-08:00","id":1165166,"title":"","content":"There's chthonians from Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T18:22:22-08:00","id":1165185,"title":"","content":"I think that more to the point than trying to classify those is to classify how they interact. Angels, Spirits and Ghosts don't interact with each other in Twilight. That means that Ephemera can exist in at least three &quot;states&quot;. Are there more states we can already address as distinct, or beings we can classify at one of those?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T19:39:17-08:00","id":1165202,"title":"","content":"i believe goetia are in their own twilight frequency too, but I don't have the mage book","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T19:46:04-08:00","id":1165205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1164981-the-list-of-ephemera?p=1165202#post1165202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i believe goetia are in their own twilight frequency too, but I don't have the mage book</div> </div> </div> </div>They would need to be given a Twilight Form Manifestation, unless you're using Psychic Genesis, which seems to create a unique Goetic. To do that requires Death or Spirit magic. It's possible that, through that magic, they would be attuned to Death or Spirit. Worth noting you can just skip Twilight Form altogether and give them a 'real' Manifestation.<br /> <br /> Further you could have any number of frequencies, as you could use any combination of Death or Spirit and another Arcana while creating an entity of some sort.<br /> <br /> There's a lot already but I expect as more books come out we'll see more 'Use ephemera rules, but they're not ephemeral,' entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-04-2017, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T19:55:08-08:00","id":1165207,"title":"","content":"But I always thought \u201cGoetia do not have Manifestations\u201d were an exception to Twilight Form?<br /> <br /> Anyways, does anyone remember how Neter-Khertet from Mummy and Amkhata worked? I think they\u2019re ephemeral (or at least pseudo-ephemeral, like Strix are), but it\u2019s been ages since I read any Mummy materials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T19:58:32-08:00","id":1165210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1164981-the-list-of-ephemera?p=1165207#post1165207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I always thought \u201cGoetia do not have Manifestations\u201d were an exception to Twilight Form?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Manifestation section, before talking about how Goetia have no Manifestations, it says 'Spirits and ghosts begin with the Twilight Form Manifestation and a number of Manifestation Effects from the list below equal to rank.' I think if they were meant to have Twilight Form it would have been mentioned there. But there is some errata and it's possible it's been cleared up. Either way, it seems like there's a Twilight frequency that can be attributed to and affected by each Arcana. P254, 'Goetia and mental projections through the Mind Arcanum are considered in phase with each other.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyways, does anyone remember how Neter-Khertet from Mummy and Amkhata worked? I think they\u2019re ephemeral (or at least pseudo-ephemeral, like Strix are), but it\u2019s been ages since I read any Mummy materials. </div> </div> </div>It's first edition, might not even have ephemera. I'll check. Yeah there's no special ephemera aspect to them, though the way they are described as 'spending much of their time immaterial, invisible, frustrated and hungry,' and it is compared to ghosts, then they start with the exceptions. 'Mostly, they're amxaibit - &quot;in shadow.&quot; But if exposed to the right sorts of occult energies, they become amxuti - &quot;in between the two horizons.&quot; Scientists studying the phenomenon use the English words &quot;tangible&quot; and &quot;intangible&quot; in casual discussion, or &quot;dephased&quot; and &quot;hard-expressing&quot; when they want to sound fancy.' Which certainly seems like Twilight but in line with my previous bleakness I'd expect it would be another 'like ephemera, but not ephemeral.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-04-2017, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T20:38:22-08:00","id":1165226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1164981-the-list-of-ephemera?p=1165210#post1165210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Manifestation section, before talking about how Goetia have no Manifestations, it says 'Spirits and ghosts begin with the Twilight Form Manifestation and a number of Manifestation Effects from the list below equal to rank.' I think if they were meant to have Twilight Form it would have been mentioned there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that the Twilight Form &quot;Manifestation&quot; is just the way that ephemeral beings exist outside of their home realms (where they don't need to manifest), I think it's safe to say that the operative part of that sentence is &quot;and a number of Manifestation Effects equal to Rank.&quot;<br /> <br /> Goetia don't normally leave the Astral but exist in Twilight when brought to the material world through summoning spells or strange confluences that don't impose a more particular state onto them. Promethean's copy of the ephemeral being mechanics includes a note about how astral projection powers technically put their users in a state of Twilight but are generally insubstantial even to each other due to lack of an ephemeral body, but that's generally representative of powers whose entire impact is the ability to move your sensory perspective freely through space rather than something with more influence; Mage's lexicon includes goetia alongside ghosts and spirits in the descriptions of what ephemera constitutes the bodies of and what ephemeral beings exist in the state of Twilight in the material world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T01:20:31-08:00","id":1165259,"title":"","content":"I reiterate from several other threads: Twilight Form might be listed as a Manifestation, but it's never treated as one by any of the rules. Goetia <i>do</i> have a Twilight Form. It's just that the writer for the ephemeral rules forgot to clarify that in the Manifestation section because even the writers doesn't treat Twilight Form as a Manifestation rather than just the default way ephemerals interact with places that has Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T15:34:56-08:00","id":1165446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1164981-the-list-of-ephemera?p=1165226#post1165226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that the Twilight Form &quot;Manifestation&quot; is just the way that ephemeral beings exist outside of their home realms (where they don't need to manifest), I think it's safe to say that the operative part of that sentence is &quot;and a number of Manifestation Effects equal to Rank.&quot;<br /> <br /> Goetia don't normally leave the Astral but exist in Twilight when brought to the material world through summoning spells or strange confluences that don't impose a more particular state onto them. Promethean's copy of the ephemeral being mechanics includes a note about how astral projection powers technically put their users in a state of Twilight but are generally insubstantial even to each other due to lack of an ephemeral body, but that's generally representative of powers whose entire impact is the ability to move your sensory perspective freely through space rather than something with more influence; Mage's lexicon includes goetia alongside ghosts and spirits in the descriptions of what ephemera constitutes the bodies of and what ephemeral beings exist in the state of Twilight in the material world.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1164981-the-list-of-ephemera?p=1165259#post1165259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I reiterate from several other threads: Twilight Form might be listed as a Manifestation, but it's never treated as one by any of the rules. Goetia <i>do</i> have a Twilight Form. It's just that the writer for the ephemeral rules forgot to clarify that in the Manifestation section because even the writers doesn't treat Twilight Form as a Manifestation rather than just the default way ephemerals interact with places that has Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if that is so simple. Probably it was on first edition, but not anymore.<br /> <br /> Once you need a Spell to bring the entity to the Material Realm, you can't say anything about its &quot;natural Twilight phase&quot;, because your spell creates such thing. As much as Twilight Form is too default to be considered the same as other Manifestations, it is still a Manifestation in the sense that it is how Ephemeral beings manifest in a non-ephemeral realm. Ghosts, Spirits and Angels can all be naturally found in the Material Realm, but in doing so exist they come in Twilight.<br /> <br /> Goetia don't do such a thing. They can't be naturally found in the Material Realm. And if a spell brings them, this same spell includes a way to &quot;Manifest&quot; them. With this, any characteristic of this manifestation can be ascribed to the spell, not the entity.<br /> <br /> But at least we can be sure of three natural-occurring Twilight Phases, and speculate solidly about one &quot;artificial&quot; Twilight Phase for each Arcana outside Spirit and Death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T16:20:52-08:00","id":1165457,"title":"","content":"It seems our disagreements are not in what Goetia are capable of and are not, but in what we each define Manifestations as, and especially in what the Twilight Form Manifestation is supposed to represent.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Contributing more to the thread, if we extend ephemera to homebrew, I\u2019m sure I\u2019ve seen someone\u2019s work on AIs as ephemeral entities in these forums. Don\u2019t remember it\u2019s name though, nor who made it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 12-05-2017, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T18:16:44-08:00","id":1165481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1164981-the-list-of-ephemera?p=1165446#post1165446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if that is so simple. Probably it was on first edition, but not anymore.<br /> <br /> Once you need a Spell to bring the entity to the Material Realm, you can't say anything about its &quot;natural Twilight phase&quot;, because your spell creates such thing. As much as Twilight Form is too default to be considered the same as other Manifestations, it is still a Manifestation in the sense that it is how Ephemeral beings manifest in a non-ephemeral realm. Ghosts, Spirits and Angels can all be naturally found in the Material Realm, but in doing so exist they come in Twilight.<br /> <br /> Goetia don't do such a thing. They can't be naturally found in the Material Realm. And if a spell brings them, this same spell includes a way to &quot;Manifest&quot; them. With this, any characteristic of this manifestation can be ascribed to the spell, not the entity.<br /> <br /> But at least we can be sure of three natural-occurring Twilight Phases, and speculate solidly about one &quot;artificial&quot; Twilight Phase for each Arcana outside Spirit and Death.</div> </div> </div> </div>But everything written about how ephemera interacts with the material world states that the natural state of ephemera is in Twilight, regardless of how it came to be in the material world. Saying that Goetia doesn't naturally have a Twilight Form is like saying people don't naturally suffocate in space. Just because we can't travel to space without tools doesn't mean suffocation isn't a very natural side effect of our presence there. (Space suits in this metaphor would be Manifestations granted through magic.)<br /> <br /> Edit: I think I get what you mean. How can we be sure that it isn't the magic that's actually giving them Twilight Form? Because Twilight Form is presented as being the default option for all ephemeral entities, including Goetia, in a section that is written from an objective standpoint rather than a character's or faction's point of view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 12-05-2017, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T18:39:58-08:00","id":1165491,"title":"","content":"Beyond making the statement that Goetia are or aren't ephemeral beings, the rest of the conversation probably deserves its own thread. And everyone seems in agreement that they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}